From 2f71935442ee747172d478a8c03b97f47a140146 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 07:19:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] radv/darwin: Phoenix 2 (Radeon 740M/760M, GC 11.0.4) canned
 table, chosen by GC version

amdgpu_devices.c gains "phoenix2": the values Linux 6.17 amdgpu and Mesa 25.2.8 reported on a Ryzen 5 8500G
(1002:15C8 rev C5): 1 SE x 1 SA x 4 CUs, 1 RB, GB_ADDR_CONFIG 0x142, external rev 0x82 (AMDGPU_PHOENIX2_RANGE),
DDR5 64-bit, 1 MiB L2, CP firmware ME 7 / PFP 14 / MEC 15, and the GC info v1.2 table of the same chip.

With a kext the handshake now picks the table from the GC IP version the kext read from the IP discovery table
(n48n_info.gc_version: 11.0.1 phoenix, 11.0.4 phoenix2), not from the PCI id; RADV_DARWIN_CANNED still overrides
it, and without a kext (HOST_BO, mock) it stays the default. acd_canned_gc_version reads the table's own
ip_discovery_version, since Phoenix 1 and 2 share the family id. Phoenix 2 is named from the CPU brand string
("Radeon 740M"), else "AMD Radeon Graphics" as on Linux.
The mock kext answers QueryInfo for RADV_DARWIN_MOCK_GC (e.g. 0xb0004) when set, so the selection by GC version
runs without hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
